# Logs
*.log
# ...except the ones under the state tree: an Evidence record's `artifact_refs` point there
# (`staging/<item>/run.log`), and an ignored file never reaches a checkout -- the hosted CI then
# found every such ref dangling while every local run was green (BUG-0069, run 36187576523).
# `tools/test_repo_hygiene.py::test_no_artifact_ref_points_at_a_file_git_ignores_bug_0069`
!project_memory/**/*.log

# Stray runtime state a measurement run drops into the repo root. Both landed in
# b32ec98 because nothing ignored them: a PowerShell module cache (a subagent ran with
# HOME pointing here) and the kit audit log, which a kit HOOK SUBPROCESS writes through
# find_repo_root() -- gate 1 never sees that write, and the item measuring the kits
# cannot forbid it.
#
# A .gitignore rule DOES NOTHING to a file git already tracks, and both of these were
# committed (b32ec98), so the rules below were dead until each file was also untracked.
# The PowerShell cache was untracked in TSK-0037 (`git rm --cached Microsoft/`); with the
# committed copy gone this rule now keeps it from being re-added. Enforced by
# tools/test_repo_hygiene.py, which fails if git tracks any file a rule here ignores.
#
# project_memory/.audit/hook_events.jsonl is STILL tracked and cannot be untracked from a
# harness session: it is canonical state under gate 1, which refuses every tool write to
# project_memory/. So for THAT file this rule is still a no-op -- it is committed and stays
# committed until the kit stops writing it. That is the open remainder H37 Rest 2 in
# docs/POST_V2_WISHLIST.md; the repair belongs in the kit, and the hygiene test excludes
# project_memory/ for exactly this reason.
Microsoft/
project_memory/.audit/

# The kernel-rendered kanban view (TSK-0071): a pure derivation of the items, rebuilt with the
# index on every state write, ~320 KB of HTML that would churn in every commit. Never tracked,
# so this rule is live from day one (unlike the two above). index.yaml STAYS tracked: rollups
# refuse to run against a state directory that holds items but no index — the board has no such
# consumer. Enforced by the same tools/test_repo_hygiene.py rule (tracked ∩ ignored must be empty).
project_memory/generated/board.html

# Office-kit TEMPLATE forms that a measuring run wrote into THIS repo's own state tree on
# 2026-08-23 (BUG-0067). This repo runs no kit and its state is dev-shaped, so an office
# onboarding form here is contamination, not state -- and the TSK-0084 verifier caught it as
# exactly the thing a `git add -A` before a delivery commit would carry into history. Ignored
# rather than deleted because project_memory/ has one writer (the kernel) and these are no
# items, so no route inside a session may remove them; BUG-0067 AC-2 carries the removal and
# AC-1 the seeding path that must stop defaulting to the repo root. Untracked from the start,
# so the rule is live immediately (tracked minus ignored stays empty -- tools/test_repo_hygiene.py).
project_memory/business_profile.yaml
project_memory/compliance_register.yaml
project_memory/content_guidelines.yaml
project_memory/filing_plan.yaml
project_memory/marketing_plan.yaml
project_memory/master_data.yaml
project_memory/product_catalog.yaml
project_memory/procedures/
